        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Birds of Steel\n- Companies: Gaijin Entertainment, Konami\n- Events: attack on Pearl Harbor\n- Places: Pearl Harbor, Wake Island\n- Topics: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- On December 7, 1941, the Empire of Japan attacked Pearl Harbor, and this attack was the immediate cause of the United States entering World War II.\n- Birds of Steel is a combat flight simulator video game created by Gaijin Entertainment and published by Konami.\n- Birds of Steel was released on March 13, 2012, for PlayStation 3 and Xbox 360.\n- Birds of Steel includes more than one hundred non-fictional planes, twenty historical missions, and hundreds of procedural missions across sixteen locations, including Pearl Harbor and Wake Island.",
